      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kensal was founded in 1892 when a train station was built near two homesteading shacks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kensal%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first bride arrived in 1893, before the original shacks were moved to farmsteads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://news.prairiepublic.org/show/dakota-datebook-archive/2022-06-09/kensal-incorporates",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A sod barn, depot, coal sheds, dwellings, and elevator sprang up after the Minnesota Loan and Trust Company laid out the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://news.prairiepublic.org/show/dakota-datebook-archive/2022-06-09/kensal-incorporates",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cecil Baker Round Barn, built in 1921, sits near Kensal and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kensal%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kensal grew along a rail line in the early 1890s, a common pattern for North Dakota towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://news.prairiepublic.org/show/dakota-datebook-archive/2022-06-09/kensal-incorporates",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A church appeared in 1893, followed by a public school, hardware store, lumberyard, bank, newspapers, and a woodmen’s lodge within the next decade.",
